IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-s2-definitions`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 6), made by the Authority with the Minister's
-- approval under section 74 of the Telecommunications Act (section 97 in the 2020 Revised Edition).
-- Texts used, all deposited under subjects/sg/telecommunications-dealers-regulations-2003/registers/source-bundle/:
--   TA1999-RG6 (the 2004 Revised Edition) and the amending regulations TA1999-RG6-S478-2005, -S396-2007, -S210-2010,
--   -S178-2011, -S251-2013, -S414-2014 and -S725-2014.
--
-- WHAT IS IN THIS FILE: the provisions that bear on who may sell, and on what a person who means to USE equipment for
-- personal purposes must obtain: reg 2 ("dealer", "telecommunication equipment"), reg 20(1) and (2) (approval for sale),
-- reg 22 (equipment for personal use, in its two forms) and item 3 of the Fifth Schedule (inserted 25 April 2013).
-- The rest of Rg 6 is in sgta-i-rg6-licensing.l4 (the 2004 Revised Edition's other provisions and Schedules) and
-- sgta-i-rg6-amendments.l4 (what each amending instrument changes).
--
-- VINTAGES.  The 2004 Revised Edition is taken as in force from 1 January 2005 (its start date is not printed in the PDF
-- and it already incorporates S 593/2004); S 478/2005 substitutes regs 20, 21 and Part VI from 21 July 2005.
-- Before 1 January 2005 -> NOTHING.
-- The last amendment on IMDA's listing is S 725/2014; the listing may not be current, so a later amendment is unknown.

§ `Rg 6 regulation 2: definitions`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:95 | "telecommunication equipment" means any appliance, apparatus or accessory
-- src:TA1999-RG6:96 | used or intended to be used for telecommunications;
@ref Rg 6 reg 2 "telecommunication equipment" (src:TA1999-RG6:95-96)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 2: this is telecommunication equipment` MEANS
    `s 2: the equipment is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` e

-- src:TA1999-RG6:78 | "dealer" means a person who manufactures, imports for sale, lets for hire, sells, or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:79 | offers or possesses for sale any equipment which is capable of being used
-- src:TA1999-RG6:80 | for the purpose of telecommunication, and includes an employee of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:81 | dealer;
@ref Rg 6 reg 2 "dealer" (src:TA1999-RG6:78-81)
GIVEN `manufactures, imports for sale, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of being used for the purpose of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 2: the person is a dealer` MEANS
    `manufactures, imports for sale, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale it` AND `it is capable of being used for the purpose of telecommunication`

§ `Rg 6 regulation 20: approval for sale`

-- 2005 form (from 21 July 2005): approval for sale is by way of registration; reg 20(2) exempts First Schedule
-- equipment that meets the Authority's published standards.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:86 | 20. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and regulation 4 (7), it shall be a condition of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:87 | licence that the licensee shall not sell —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:88 | (a) any type of telecommunication equipment to be used for connection to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:89 | any telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:90 | telecommunication system licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:91 | (b) any type of radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:92 | unless the type of equipment has been approved for sale by way of registration with
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:93 | the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:94 | (2) No approval for sale under paragraph (1) is required for any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:95 | telecommunication equipment which is —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:96 | (a) set out in the First Schedule; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:97 | (b) designed and constructed in accordance with such standards and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:98 | specifications as may be published by the Authority.
@ref Rg 6 reg 20(1) and (2) as substituted by S 478/2005 (src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:86-98)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the equipment is to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is set out in the First Schedule and designed and constructed in accordance with the standards and specifications the Authority publishes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(1) and (2) (from 21 July 2005): approval for sale by registration is required` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               JUST (    (   `the equipment is to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee`
                          OR `the equipment is radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore`)
                     AND (NOT `it is set out in the First Schedule and designed and constructed in accordance with the standards and specifications the Authority publishes`))

§ `Rg 6 regulation 22: telecommunication equipment for personal use`

-- 2004 Revised Edition form (before 21 July 2005): the Authority may TEST equipment at the request of a person who
-- intends to use it for personal purposes.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:381 | 22. —(1) The Authority may, at the request of any person intending to use any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:382 | telecommunication equipment or type of telecommunication equipment for personal
-- src:TA1999-RG6:383 | purpose, test that equipment to verify that the equipment is designed, constructed,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:384 | installed, established, maintained or operated in accordance with such technical
-- src:TA1999-RG6:385 | specifications as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:386 | (2) The Authority may, in its discretion, impose the fees specified in the Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:387 | (3) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to any radio-communication equipment that is not
-- src:TA1999-RG6:388 | type-approved equipment.
@ref Rg 6 reg 22, 2004 Revised Edition (src:TA1999-RG6:381-388)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person asks the Authority to test the equipment, intending to use it for personal purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment that is not type-approved equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 22 (2004 Revised Edition form): the Authority may test the equipment at the person's request` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 1 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN
               JUST (`the person asks the Authority to test the equipment, intending to use it for personal purposes` AND (NOT `the equipment is radio-communication equipment that is not type-approved equipment`))
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Form substituted by S 478/2005 (from 21 July 2005): a person intending to use telecommunication equipment for personal
-- purposes is not required to obtain the Authority's approval, PROVIDED the equipment is designed, constructed,
-- installed, established, maintained and operated in accordance with the standards and specifications the Authority
-- publishes.  The Authority may, in its discretion, require the person to cease operating it or to send it for testing.
-- FORK 4 (recorded in TV-QUESTION.md section 4; NOTES.md points there): what this "approval" is.  Reading X: it is the approval for connection and use of
-- s 11 and nothing else, so reg 22(1) says nothing about a licence under s 5 or about s 54(1).  Reading Y: reg 22(1) is a
-- regulation made under the Act that regulates personal use, so possession in accordance with it is "in accordance with
-- ... any regulations made under this Act" (s 54(1)).  This module records what reg 22(1) says; which reading the seat
-- layer applies is recorded where it is applied.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:145 | 22. —(1) Any person intending to use any telecommunication equipment for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:146 | personal purposes shall not be required to obtain the approval of the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:147 | provided that such equipment is designed, constructed, installed, established,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:148 | maintained and operated in accordance with such standards and specifications as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:149 | may be published by the Authority.
@ref Rg 6 reg 22(1) as substituted by S 478/2005 (src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:145-149)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person intends to use the telecommunication equipment for personal purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is designed, constructed, installed, established, maintained and operated in accordance with the standards and specifications the Authority publishes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 22(1) (from 21 July 2005): the person is not required to obtain the approval of the Authority` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               JUST (    `the person intends to use the telecommunication equipment for personal purposes`
                     AND `the equipment is designed, constructed, installed, established, maintained and operated in accordance with the standards and specifications the Authority publishes`)

-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:150 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Authority may, in its discretion, require
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:151 | any such person —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:152 | (a) to cease operating any such telecommunication equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:153 | (b) to send, at his own expense, any such telecommunication equipment for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:154 | certification or testing by any local or foreign body specified by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:155 | Authority.”.
@ref Rg 6 reg 22(2) as substituted by S 478/2005 (src:TA1999-RG6-S478-2005:150-155)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Authority requires the person to cease operating the equipment or to send it for certification or testing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 22(2) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority has exercised its discretion` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Authority requires the person to cease operating the equipment or to send it for certification or testing`

§ `Rg 6 Fifth Schedule: equipment for which registration and renewal fees do not apply`

-- Item 3 was inserted by S 251/2013 from 25 April 2013.  The Fifth Schedule from S 210/2010 (15 April 2010) lists items
-- 1 and 2 only.  Its heading says what it is for: registration and renewal-of-registration FEES do not apply.
-- Before 15 April 2010 the Fifth Schedule was a different schedule (fees for tests on equipment for personal use) and is
-- not modelled: NOTHING.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:18 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:19 | (Dealers) (Amendment) Regulations 2013 and shall come into
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:20 | operation on 25th April 2013.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:161 | (b) by inserting, immediately after item 2, the following item:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:163 | 3. Integrated receiver Not applicable Not applicable
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:164 | decoder devices intended
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:165 | for use with second
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:166 | generation digital
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:167 | terrestrial television
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:168 | broadcasting system
@ref Rg 6 Fifth Schedule item 3 inserted by S 251/2013 (src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:18-20; src:TA1999-RG6-S251-2013:161-168)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is an integrated receiver decoder device intended for use with the second generation digital terrestrial television broadcasting system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Fifth Schedule: item 3 lists this equipment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 15 4 2010) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 25 4 2013) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST `it is an integrated receiver decoder device intended for use with the second generation digital terrestrial television broadcasting system`
